== cfb-dynasty-390-anim
  cfb-dynasty-390-anim pick line: Every new dynasty comes with an athletic director: he sets an ask each season and grades it.
  cfb-dynasty-390-anim card: Back THE ATHLETIC DIRECTOR'S ASK, 2026 Make the Playoff and win a Playoff game. The boosters paid for this roster. Trust upstairs 60 of 100 In the postseason picture. Hold it. YOUR RECORD Alabama, since 2026 0 seasons, 0 titles
  cfb-dynasty-390-anim rules: Back How the athletic director works Before every season the athletic director names an ask, read off where your roster ranks in the country, not off the program's name. In this game the athletic director asks one step less of every roster that would be asked for a postseason result, because only 12 of 44 programs make the Playoff and one loss ends a run there: the best rosters are asked to make the Playoff and win a Playoff game, the next ones to make it, and nobody is asked for the national title outright. Trust starts at 60 of 100. At the end of every season it moves by the grade: +40 for the national title, +22 for beating the ask, +14 for meeting it, -16 for falling short and -28 for missing it by a mile. Trust at zero and you are let go. The dynasty does not end there: the phone rings with the jobs you have earned, or nobody calls and you can sit a year out while the country plays on. If the phone stops for good, a new dynasty is the way back in. Let go straight after a season nowhere near the ask and no program above the second tier will call. A program that let you go never calls again. Those are this game's rules. Sit a year out and the program that let you go plays the season with nobody in your chair, so a coordinator it loses that offseason stays unreplaced until the next one. A big year gets noticed. Win the national title at a program below the top tier and a program one tier up pays your buyout to bring you over 60 times in 100; beat the ask and it happens 35 times in 100. Go, or stay put. That is this game's rule, not a claim about how real schools hire. A WORKED EXAMPLE Say you take over with trust 60 and fall short of the ask: 60 -16 leaves 44. Next season you miss it by a mile: 44 -28 leaves 16, and the seat is hot. Do it again and trust hits 0: you are let go, and the job market opens.
  cfb-dynasty-390-anim old save round 4: slot=passed text="NO ATHLETIC DIRECTOR THIS SEASON One can take the job at the start of next season."
  cfb-dynasty-390-anim See who calls 120 ms after the final press: {"vis":"hidden","op":"0","x":195,"y":804}
  cfb-dynasty-390-anim fired: The athletic director let you go 🔻 Nowhere near the ask. The athletic director stopped returning calls. The athletic director let you go after 1 season and no titles at Alabama. Nobody called this year. The phone can still ring next year, and every year out makes it quieter.
  cfb-dynasty-390-anim market (as fired): Out of work The athletic director let you go after 1 season and no titles at Alabama. Nobody called this year. The phone can still ring next year, and every year out makes it quieter. Sit the year out Start a new dynasty YOUR RECORD Alabama, since 2026 1 season, 0 titles, let go
  cfb-dynasty-390-anim year out: season 2026 to 2027, seasonsOut 0 to 1, phase recap, titles 0 to 0, played 1 to 1
  cfb-dynasty-390-anim market after the year out: The phone has stopped 1 season out of work since Alabama let you go. Nobody called, and nobody will: the phone has stopped. A new dynasty is the way back in. The country played 2027 without you, and Notre Dame won the national title. Start a new dynasty YOUR RECORD Alabama, since 2026 1 season, 0 titles, let go
  cfb-dynasty-390-anim the engine's champion of 2027: ND
  cfb-dynasty-390-anim first offer: Boise Statebottom tier program / Prestige 78, roster #27 of 44, 10-3 last season / Win 5 games and give the boosters a reason to keep writing checks. / They want someone who has won the national title more than once.
  cfb-dynasty-390-anim took a job: ALA to BSU, stints 1 to 2, phase recruit, new stint from 2028, season 2027, mandate 2028 "Win 5 games and give the boosters a reason to keep writing checks."
  cfb-dynasty-390-anim the new program's tile: ATHLETIC DIRECTOR TRUST 60 Win 5 games and give the boosters a reason to keep writing checks. 0 wins keeps the mandate on pace.
  cfb-dynasty-390-anim first season at BSU: grades ["overachieved"], trust 82, recap line "📈 Ahead of the ask. The athletic director noticed, and so did everybody else. Trust upstairs: 82 of 100" fired 0
